On Sunday's Last Week Tonight , John Oliver channeled the anger felt by millions of Americans at last week's nationwide FAA ground stop .

Oliver noted that official information was fairly scarce during most of the five hours when some 3,500 planes were grounded. He then suggested that, when they finally did appear on TV, Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy and Secretary of Homeland Security Markwayne Mullin weren't quite up to the task of explaining the situation to Americans.

After calling Mullin a &#8220;moron,&#8221; Oliver had this for Duffy: &#8220;Rather than use that press conference to dispense information, which would have been ideal, he instead took it as an opportunity to air grievances and make demands.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); } Related Stories News Networks Scramble To Report On Reasons Behind "Extraordinary" Nationwide Ground Stop Of All U.S. Flights News John Oliver Unleashes Withering Critique Of Pete Hegseth On 'Last Week Tonight'

The show then cut to a clip of Duffy.

&#8220;What went down was old. It was old, legacy equipment that failed,&#8221; said the secretary. &#8220;And, listen, it's going to continue to fail&#8230;The president for the last year has been asking Congress to fully fund a full build of a brand new air traffic control system&#8230;The president's asked for $30B. I want $50B. I can't build things if i don't have money&#8230;I want &50B. President Trump is a builder. He is going to build this network for the American people.&#8221;

Oliver couldn't contain himself.

&#8220;What are you doing going on TV to demand $50B?!&#8221; he asked. &#8220;You sound less like a secretary of transportation trying to calm people down and more like a Batman villain trying to hold Gotham hostage! &#8216;I need $50B unless the Batman can solve my riddles in time!'&#8221;

Oliver admitted that Duffy is right about one thing: U.S. flight systems are outdated. But the Last Week Tonight host pointed out that Republicans have had both houses of Congress (and the presidency) for the past two years, so if there's a complaint about underfunding, it should land on their collective doorstep. He also pointed out that the Republican Congress and the administration collaborated to nearly triple ICE's budget last year to $28B, an amount that surpasses the annual budgets of almost all other major federal law enforcement agencies combined. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Oliver then went in for the kill.

&#8220;It is hard to take a panicked shakedown from Duffy, not just because his cost estimate jumped by $20B mid-sentence, but also because he's part of a flagrantly-corrupt administration who spent a chunk of his time in office shooting a shitty reality show with his family to encourage Americans to take more road trips.&#8221; [Duffy, his wife and their nine kids shot The Great American Road Trip over seven months this year and last.]

&#8220;To that end,&#8221; said Oliver in reference to both the show and the recent flight stoppage, &#8220;guess what, Sean? Mission f*cking accomplished!&#8221;

Five giants of the global film community were feted on Sunday night at the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences' 17th annual Governors Awards : actress Glenn Close , animator Floyd Norman and &#x2014; in absentia due to a recent medical procedure &#x2014; director/producer Ridley Scott with bestowed honorary Oscars, and longtime indie producing partners Christine Vachon and Pamela Koffler with the Irving G. Thalberg Memorial Award, which recognizes &#8220;creative producers whose bodies of work reflect a consistently high quality of motion picture production.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The black-tie gathering, which took place inside the Ray Dolby Ballroom at Ovation Hollywood, was, as always, packed with Academy members &#x2014; including most of the 55 members of the organization's board of governors , who host the event &#x2014; and dozens of current Oscar contenders. Among them: You Can See Everything 's Nathan Fielder and Lance Oppenheim, The Odyssey 's Christopher Nolan, Zendaya, Tom Holland and Charlize Theron, The Debut 's Julianne Moore, Paul Giamatti and Emma Stone, Obsession 's Curry Barker and Inde Navarrette, Elsinore 's Andrew Scott, The Invite 's Olivia Wilde and Pen&#xE9;lope Cruz, Wild Horse Nine 's John Malkovich, Artificial 's Andrew Garfield and Monica Barbaro, and Dune: Part Three 's Timoth&#xE9;e Chalamet, accompanied by Kylie Jenner. Related Stories TV Kids' Choice Awards: 'Spider-Man: Brand New Day,' Zendaya, Tom Holland, BTS Among 2026 Winners Movies 'Fatherland' Wins Top Camerimage Prize as 'Wild Horse Nine' Nabs Audience Award

Seated with Scott were his family, along with Lucy Fisher, Doug Wick, Jim Gianopulos, Tom Rothman, Richard Lovett, Simon Halls, Steve Asbell, Matt Damon and Jerry Bruckheimer, while Norman was notably joined by Marlon West and Travon Free. Close's table consisted of Malkovich, Kevin Huvane, Franklin Latt, Rodrigo Garcia and Ram Bergman. Vachon and Koffler were accompanied by John Sloss, Wash Westmoreland, Marcus Hu and Liz Karlsen. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The first awardee was Norman, 91, who began his career in 1956 at Walt Disney Animation Studios as the company's first Black animator. He contributed to numerous Disney classics including Sleeping Beauty , The Sword in the Stone , Mary Poppins , The Jungle Book and Robin Hood , as well as other notable films made outside of the Mouse House including The Hunchback of Notre Dame , Mulan , Monsters, Inc. and Toy Story 2 . A friend and mentor to younger animators and storyboard artists, he was the subject of a 2016 documentary feature, Floyd Norman: An Animated Life .

The presentation of the honorary Oscar to Norman &#x2014;&#xA0;only the fourth animator to ever receive that accolade, after Walter Lantz, Chuck Jones and Hayao Miyazaki &#x2014; was led by Your Mother Your Mother Your Mother star Mahershala Ali, who stated, &#8220;Floyd has played a pivotal role in our lives without any of us even realizing it, one [animation] at a time."

In his acceptance speech, Norman reflected on his beginnings in the industry, offering &#8220;a special thank you to the best mentor a filmmaker could ever have, Walt Disney." He concluded his speech remarking, "On occasion, even movies have a happy ending. This special evening? Here's my happy ending."

The evening's next honoree was Close, one of the great stars and character actresses of the past 50 years. The 79-year-old has received eight Oscar nominations, four for leading performances (1987's Fatal Attraction , 1988's Dangerous Liaisons , 2011's Albert Nobbs and 2018's The Wife ) and four for supporting turns (1982's The World According to Garp , 1983's The Big Chill , 1984's The Natural and 2020's Hillbilly Elegy ). She could just as easily have been nominated for 1985's Jagged Edge and Maxie , 1990's Reversal of Fortune , 1994's The Paper , 1996's 101 Dalmatians and 1997's Air Force One . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Close's tally of eight noms for performances is higher than that of all but three other actresses, dead or alive &#x2014; Meryl Streep (21), Katharine Hepburn (12) and Bette Davis (11), each of whom won multiple times &#x2014; and more than any other living man or woman (Peter O'Toole, who died in 2013, also went 0-for-eight and received an honorary Oscar).

The presentation of the honorary Oscar to Close &#x2014; who previously presented honorary Oscars to the National Endowment for the Arts in 1985, Deborah Kerr in 1994 and Carol Littleton in 2023 &#x2014; was kicked off by John Malkovich, who described her as &#8220;my friend and treasured colleague.&#8221; Close's Dangerous Liaisons co-star then went on to state, "She is a true master&#x2026; she's got the goods, she can do the big stuff, the little stuff, and everything in between&#x2026; Glenn is unafraid to &#x2018;go there,' and I love that about her,&#8221; Malkovich added. &#8220;She loves the world, she is relentless, very smart, a little cagey and a great actress who knows exactly what she's doing and gives it 100 percent every single time."

Following a lengthy standing ovation, Close, who dedicated the award to her daughter, Annie, declared: &#8220;As an outsider, I have never worried about whether I was going to win or not, though some years I thought I might have a chance. I have always felt that the great honor is to be in the room. Over the past 43 years, I've been in the room eight times&#8230; so to be in this room tonight, embraced by the people who have consistently inspired me, whose work has sustained and challenged me and only made me want to be better is the greatest honor of all.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Next up was Scott, whose films, collectively, have been nominated for 45 Oscars and won nine, but who himself has never won a competitive Oscar. The 88-year-old, who was nearly 40 when he made his directorial debut, has made up &#x2014; and continues to make up &#x2014; for lost time, consistently pumping out action-packed blockbusters, many now considered landmarks of cinematic achievement.

Indeed, he is behind two of the most significant sci-fi films of all time, 1979's Alien and 1982's Blade Runner , as well as 1991's Thelma & Louise (for which he received a best director Oscar nom), 2000's Gladiator (which won the best picture Oscar, while he lost best director), 2001's Black Hawk Down (for which he received his most recent best director Oscar nom) and 2015's The Martian . He has also produced many of his films, as well as a ton of TV series.

The presentation of the honorary Oscar to Scott was led by Matt Damon, who described him as "a master at the helm" of two films they've made together, The Martian and The Last Duel , stating, "Thank you to the Academy on behalf of everyone who has ever worked with Ridley Scott. It is about time we all saw him with an Academy Award in his hand." Scott accepted his Oscar via a pre-recorded video from London, which included a clip from his first movie, Boy in a Bicycle , featuring his late brother, Tony, in which the narrator states, &#8220;I'll remember this moment when I'm 80, and it'll all seem like yesterday.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid4' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#8220;That was a moment for both of us,&#8221; Scott stated. &#8220;Now I'm well past 80, and I've thought about those days and moments. It does resonate just like yesterday. Both of us sharing our first film together that led to 20 years of advertising, five decades of filmmaking&#8230; I'm flattered and proud to accept this award, but I also accept it for Tony. His great work would certainly have earned this recognition.&#8221;

The final awardees of the night were Vachon, 63, and Koffler, 60, two of the most important producers in the history of American independent film. The co-founders of New York-based Killer Films have guided to fruition all 10 of Todd Haynes' features &#x2014; including Poison (1991), Safe (1995), Far from Heaven (2002) and Carol (2015) &#x2014; plus Larry Clark's Kids (1995), Todd Solondz's Happiness (1998), Kimberly Peirce's Boys Don't Cry (1999), John Cameron Mitchell's Hedwig and the Angry Inch (2001), Wash Westmoreland and Richard Glatzer's Still Alice (2014) and Celine Song's Past Lives (2023, for which they received their sole Oscar noms).

Vachon, the more public-facing of the duo, has been nicknamed &#8220;the Queen of New Queer Cinema&#8221; and is such a fixture of the indie scene that she was affectionately referenced alongside Spike Lee, Michael Moore and Richard Linklater in the title of the classic 1996 tome Spike, Mike, Slackers, & Dykes: A Guided Tour Across a Decade of American Independent Cinema . Her own 2006 book A Killer Life , which she co-wrote with Austin Bunn, was included on The Hollywood Reporter &#8216;s 2023 list of the 100 greatest film books of all time . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid5' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The presentation of the Thalberg to Vachon and Koffler was kicked off by Neil Patrick Harris with a performance from Hedwig and the Angry Inch , which Vachon and Koffler produced. Todd Haynes and Julianne Moore then conducted the actual handoff of the statuettes.

Russell Brand has shared a message from prison, delivered by his wife, Laura Brand, on his YouTube channel Sunday.

&#8220;So Russell has asked me to read something to you today,&#8221; she said at the beginning of the video, before looking to a notebook to read her husband's message. &#8220;Beloved brothers and sisters in Christ, God bless you for your support. As you know, I am not guilty for the offenses I have been jailed for, so something strange is happening.&#8221;

Brand was sentenced to 10 years and six months in prison after being found guilty of rape and sexual assault last Monday. The trial lasted four weeks at Southwark Crown Court, with the jury finding him guilty on one count of rape and three counts of sexual assault (he was found not guilty on two other rape charges and not guilty of attempted indecent assault). blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Movies Listen to the River! 'Arrow for a Stone Heart' Is a Poetic Experience Told Through an Indigenous Lens Movies 'Fatherland' Wins Top Camerimage Prize as 'Wild Horse Nine' Nabs Audience Award

Laura continued to deliver Russell's message, reading, &#8220;The good news is that Christ is with us when we choose him, and I do. I am incarcerated in HMP Littlehey. Little as in small, and hey as in, &#x2018;Hey, I'm in the biggest sex offenders prison in Europe.' The good news is that I have already seen that the staff here are strong, they are kind, and they are dedicated. And as for my fellow prisoners, I now know that I am in no position to judge anyone.&#8221;

"I don't know which other men here are not guilty, and the ones that are, they are people that Christ died to save, like you and me. Let us all love, pray for, and forgive one another as God forgave us. Please support my treasured wife and family. I feel your prayers. Your brother in Christ, Russell,&#8221; the remarks concluded. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In a pre-recorded portion of the YouTube video, Russell compared the coverage of his trial to that of a &#8220;football match.&#8221;

"So obviously, as I said last week, we're in the middle of a trial," he said. "I mean, we don't really look at coverage, but someone showed me some of the coverage the other day from people that were actually broadly supportive. But I know that's not generally how it's being covered in the mainstream media, and you can draw your own conclusions from that. Although what I will say is, it's amazing to watch other people's coverage of it because they just talk about it like it's a football match."

In a new report from The Times and Netflix's Russell Brand: Open Secret documentary, six more women accused of him of alleged sexual misconduct.

